# Computer Network

A computer network is a group of devices connected together to share information and resources.

Examples of network devices:
- Computers
- Smartphones
- Servers
- Routers
- Switches
- Printers

---

# Types of Networks

## PAN (Personal Area Network)

Small network around one person.

Example:
Bluetooth between a phone and wireless earbuds.

---

## LAN (Local Area Network)

Covers a small geographical area.

Examples:
- Home
- Office
- School

---

## MAN (Metropolitan Area Network)

Connects multiple LANs across a city.

Example:
University campuses.

---

## WAN (Wide Area Network)

Connects networks over large distances.

Example:
The Internet.

---

# Network Devices

## Router

- Connects different networks.
- Routes packets.
- Works at OSI Layer 3.

---

## Switch

- Connects devices within the same LAN.
- Uses MAC addresses.
- Works at OSI Layer 2.

---

## Modem

- Connects a network to an Internet Service Provider (ISP).

---

## Access Point (AP)

Provides wireless network connectivity.

---

# Network Topologies

## Bus

One shared cable.

Pros:
- Cheap

Cons:
- Single cable failure affects the network.

---

## Star

All devices connect to a central switch.

Pros:
- Easy to troubleshoot.
- Most common.

Cons:
- Central device failure affects all connected devices.

---

## Ring

Devices form a circle.

Pros:
- Organized communication.

Cons:
- One failure can interrupt communication.

---

## Mesh

Every device connects to every other device.

Pros:
- High redundancy.

Cons:
- Expensive.

---

## Hybrid

Combination of different topologies.

Used in large organizations.

